 ```
 
+## Create-user endpoint
+
+`CreateUserEndpoint.Handle` parses a raw JSON body and returns either `CreateUserOutcome.Accepted` (respond 201) or `CreateUserOutcome.Rejected` carrying an RFC 9457 problem document (respond 400 with its `Status`, `Title`, and `Errors`).
+
+| Payload | Outcome | Problem title |
+|---|---|---|
+| JSON object with valid fields | `Accepted` | — |
+| Missing, `null`, or blank body | `Rejected` | `Missing request body` |
+| Invalid JSON, JSON that is not an object, or wrong field types | `Rejected` | `Malformed request body` |
+| Parsed body failing `Validator` | `Rejected` | `Request validation failed` |
+
+`Example.Tests/CreateUserEndpointTests.cs` covers the valid, missing, and malformed payload cases.
